  "chitchat": [
    "drops the hood and lays down a bead without hurrying.",
    "\"We make it, we mend it, we don't ask. That last one is the popular bit.\"",
    "\"Don't watch the arc. You will be seeing it again at three in the morning.\""
  ],
  "description": "A short, wide welder with forearms like plumbing and a hood he flips up rather than takes off, so he mostly sees the world through a slot. Every visible inch of him is dotted with old spark burns and he treats them as punctuation.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "\"Right. Mind the offcuts. They are sharper than they look and so am I.\""
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Just passing.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Doughty flips the hood up and squints at you through the after-image. \"If it is bent, leave it on the bench. If it is a person, leave it outside.\""
    }
  },
